WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.566
The data was captured with a Clearpath Husky
unmanned ground vehicle,

00:00:04.646 --> 00:00:07.327
remotely operated through downtown Seoul.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:10.962
The robot carried two sixteen-channel Velodyne LiDARs,

00:00:11.042 --> 00:00:14.800
five Basler cameras arranged to cover a full 360 degrees,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.379
two inertial measurement units, and real-time
kinematic positioning.

00:00:19.459 --> 00:00:21.668
To fuse camera and LiDAR reliably,

00:00:21.748 --> 00:00:28.738
a pulse-per-second signal generator triggers all
the sensors so their data is accurately aligned in time.

00:00:28.818 --> 00:00:35.539
The robot's own pose is recovered from RTK outdoors
and from a LiDAR-inertial SLAM algorithm indoors,

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:41.800
which is needed to compensate for the robot's
ego-motion when forming pedestrian trajectories

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.888
and to align the semantic maps.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:50.554
Those maps use a twelve-layer hierarchical
structure built from point clouds and segmented by hand.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:53.988
Expert annotators labeled 3D cuboids at five hertz,

00:00:54.068 --> 00:00:56.681
which were interpolated up to ten hertz,

00:00:56.761 --> 00:01:01.394
and 2D boxes were generated from the 3D cuboids
that share object IDs.

00:01:01.474 --> 00:01:05.030
For privacy, all faces and license plates are blurred.
